":20,\"named\":20}],[\"http://pragma.canonical.com/codestandards#CodeStandard\",{\"total\":149,\"named\":149}],[\"https://dt.canonical.com/Coordinate\",{\"total\":36,\"named\":36}]],\"selfReferential\":[\"http://pragma.canonical.com/codestandards#extends\",\"https://ds.canonical.com/parentComponent\",\"https://ds.canonical.com/hasSubcomponent\"],\"functionalViolations\":[],\"undeclaredPredicates\":[\"https://ds.canonical.com/hasImplementation\",\"https://ds.canonical.com/implementationCount\"],\"annotations\":[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/content\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance\",\"Write the concept as a complete Markdown document: open with what it is and why it matters, then cover the guidance in structured sections with concrete, real-world examples.\"],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Should be a self-contained Markdown document that fully explains the concept, with clear sections and concrete examples. May reference UIBlocks and other concepts by name or link.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance\",\"Provide detailed guidelines for correctly using and implementing the UI block. Include best practices for accessibility, responsiveness, content handling, localization, animation, and keyboard interaction. Ensure that the guidelines are comprehensive and cover all important aspects of using and implementing the component correctly.\"],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"These guidelines should contain the best practices for accessibility, responsiveness, content handling, localization, animation and keyboard interaction of this UI block. They should be comprehensive and cover all important aspects of using and implementing the component correctly.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/usage\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance\",\"Document when and when not to use the component, with a short general description. Cover all use cases and anti-patterns distinctly, name the alternative component for discouraged uses, and draw examples from real released usage.\"],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Should include a general description and clear When-to-use / When-not-to-use guidance. Each scenario should be distinct; when discouraging a use, name the component to use instead. All variants should be considered. Examples should be drawn from real-world, released usage.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/tier\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance\",\"Assign the UI block to a specific tier within the design system. Choose from predefined tier values such as core, global, global_form, apps, site, etc. This property is mandatory and should have only one value.\"],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Has to be mandatory and singular. Must be one of the predefined tier values (core, global, global_form, apps, site, etc.).\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/decisionLog\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance\",\"Document any decisions made regarding the entity, including the date of the decision, the author responsible for the decision, and a clear explanation of the change or decision made. This log helps maintain a history of changes and the rationale behind them.\"],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"[date] Contains the date of the decision made, [author] Links to the decision maker, [content] Contains the reasons of change, is clear on what the change is\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/version\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance\",\"Provide a semantic version number following the MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH format (e.g., 1.0.0, 2.1.3). Include optional pre-release identifiers (e.g., 1.0.0-alpha) and build metadata (e.g., 1.0.0+build.123456789).\"],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must follow semantic versioning format: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH with optional pre-release and build metadata\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/summary\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance\",\"Write an introduction that gives a quick overview of the entity. Start with the primary purpose and list all the main use cases. Make sure to include information that can help users decide if this is the right element they need.\"],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Concise paragraph (3-5 sentences) that clearly describes the purpose of the entity, lists at least 2-3 use cases, and is written in a clear and accessible way. Enables readers to quickly determine if this is the right component for their needs.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/name\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance\",\"Provide a clear and descriptive name for the entity that accurately reflects its purpose and functionality within the design system.\"],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a concise, descriptive name that clearly identifies the entity. Should be unique within the design system and avoid generic terms like 'button' or 'input' without context.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/rank\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a positive integer no greater than the length of the tuple's anatomy:consumes list.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/node\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"A role alone would collide: global.pattern.table_of_contents binds role 'link' at three depths with identical styles.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/viaBlock\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Part of the record's identity, not an attribute: a block's own root binding and one inherited from a subcomponent's root share node, key, state and rank.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/consumesSymbol\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must name a symbol declared in S1 or minted into S2, unless anatomies/register.yaml admits the element under X1, X2, X5, X7 or X15.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/hasTokenBinding\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Derived; one record per identity tuple, so a subcomponent referenced twice yields one record and not two.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Derived by deriveTokenBindings from the block's ds:anatomyDsl literal and the transitive closure of its uri: references. Never hand-asserted.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/libraryTier\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must reference a valid ds:Tier instance\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/documentation\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a valid URL\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/link\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a valid URL\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/platform\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Should be a recognised platform name\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/libraryName\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must match the published package identifier\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/isDraft\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be true or false\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/importStatement\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a complete import statement naming the published package specifier and an export the package really provides. ABSENT rather than guessed when the implementation is not reachable by name from the library's entry point — a subcomponent published only as a property of its parent (Breadcrumbs.Item) or an internal file carries none.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/versionedLink\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a valid URL including version tag\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/headLink\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a valid URL\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/library\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must reference a valid ds:ImplementationLibrary instance\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/implementationVersion\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Should follow semver format\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/implementsBlock\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must reference a valid ds:UIBlock instance\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/constraints\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Should describe the valid value space for this property. Format varies by property type.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/defaultValue\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a valid value for the property's type\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/optional\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be true or false\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/propertyType\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be one of the recognised type values used across the design system\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/targetDevices\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Comma-separated list of device categories (e.g. desktop, tablet, mobile)\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/timestamp\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a valid ISO-8601 dateTime\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/gridAreas\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be valid CSS grid-area names matching the grid template\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/domain\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Should describe the category of content the layout organises (e.g. documentation, dashboard, settings)\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/grid\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a valid CSS grid-template value or shorthand\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/hasSubcomponent\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Inverse of ds:parentComponent. Each referenced entity must be a ds:Subcomponent.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/parentComponent\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must reference a valid ds:Component instance\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/standalone\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be true or false. When true, the subcomponent may appear in UIs without its parent.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/inheritsFrom\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must reference a valid ds:UIBlock that this block specialises, and must follow the rules of inheritance (to be specified in full later). One such rule: the inheriting block's name is the parent block's name with a prefix applied (e.g. Tooltip -> DataTooltip, Button -> DropdownButton). Should not be cyclic.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be valid YAML conforming to the Anatomy DSL specification. Root node must be named (have uri). See skills/anatomy-author/SKILL.md for format.\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Identifies all significant UI block parts and their relationships. Parts are decomposed only to the level where they are meaningful and reusable (e.g., if a component is made of other published components, reference those components instead of redescribing them). Each part is assigned a descriptive name, visual slot and description of its role in the overall component structure. Relationships between parts are documented: cardinality (1, 0..1, 1..*) and nesting (which parts are contained within others). Includes visual annotations or diagrams showing the anatomical structure. Both visual representation and text list align and describe the same parts. No orphaned or unnamed parts—every element in the anatomy is accounted for\"]]],[\"https://ds.canonical.com/figmaLink\",[[\"https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria\",\"Must be a valid URL pointing to the Figma design file for this UI block. The URL should be accessible and correctly formatted.\"]]]],\"deepBlankNesting\":true,\"graphqlAnnotations\":[[\"https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri\",\"https://pragma.canonical.com/graphql#name\",\"anatomyUri\",\"literal\"]]}";
